 on your body so what  tips do you have to stay motivated as we  transition into those darker evenings  and colder mornings well you know what's  so interesting for me it's always  finding my thing that i enjoy so for  example this may sound crazy i'm an avid  reader i love reading so at nights i  reward myself with a cup of tea  and i get to sit down with my iphone and  i pick a book and i love to read so it's  all about going back to the basics  sometimes finding that thing if you have  a favorite food you love another thing  that i'm a huge advocate of is a sun  lamp right especially where if you  struggle with some sort of seasonal  thing i happen to you know most of my  life and so a sun lamp is really awesome  for me making sure you get out and get  enough sunshine because it helps your  production you know your vitamin d and  helps you stay motivated yeah absolutely  and in las vegas we're so used to sun  all the time and then when that's gone  it's a big adjustment for it's huge you  don't recognize it well thank you so  much for all the tips and if anyone  wants to read more or learn more where  can they find you you know what just  find us on everyday woman is our brand  we have a huge community of over 14 000  women just look for us on facebook you  can go to everydaywoman.me and check it  out we have all kinds of tips for women  so well thank you so much angela we're  all excited for fall so thank you for  all the tips i'll send it over to  mercedes
 

